    "authors_reviews": [
      {
        "position": 1,
        "title": "Great bath brush",
        "text": "This brush is a soft silicone, but not so soft it collapses when you use it. It scrubs through my puppy’s medium-thick fur and gets a solid lather going without scratching. He hasn’t fully lost his puppy coat yet so verdict is still out on long-term effectiveness, but so far so good. The two sides have different length teeth, which is great for reaching both the top coat and the fluff underneath. It’s comfortable to hold (might be a tad slippery if you have smaller hands) and easy to rinse clean.My puppy tolerates it pretty well, keeping in mind that he’s still at the stage where he thinks everything in the world is either food or a chew toy. (They grow out of that, right? ...Right?) Honestly, it works well enough that I’m half-tempted to hand it to my kid, who has about the same hair density and washing enthusiasm. But I won’t. Probably.Bottom line: Great design, easy to use, and gets the job done.",
        "rating": 5,
        "date": "November 10, 2025",
        "author": "Steph",
        "author_link": "https://www.amazon.com/gp/profile/amzn1.account.AG4RKLI4CV4HIA6J7KAL3PLE6ZEA?ref=cm_cr_dp_d_bdcrb_top",
        "author_image": "https://m.media-amazon.com/images/S/amazon-avatars-global/default._SX48_.png",
        "product": {
          "color": "Black"
        }
      },
      {
        "position": 2,
        "title": "A little ruff for small dogs.",
        "text": "I'll start out with saying, our dog is on the very small end of the scale. He's a wonderful little 8 pound Havanese with medium length hair. He does very well in a bath, but it can sometimes be a challenge getting a good scrub of the little guy. So, we gave these a shot.In general, these are very easy to use. They seem very durable and I would expect them to last quite a long time. The bristles are firm to the point they retain their shape well, but the geometry provides a soft brushing to the dog.I expect these would work very well for a larger dog (30 lb and above). But for our pup, these are were over sized and ended up being a little cumbersome to use.For the money, these would be a nice value for an appropriately sized dog. For small dogs, you should probably look for something else.",
        "rating": 4,
        "date": "October 7, 2025",
        "author": "Dan",
        "author_link": "https://www.amazon.com/gp/profile/amzn1.account.AGNWVVDI5KHV6LJLPCGJ7L4BUIOQ?ref=cm_cr_dp_d_bdcrb_top",
        "author_image": "https://m.media-amazon.com/images/S/amazon-avatars-global/default._SX48_.png",
        "images": [
          "https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/71I+oxgH4HL.jpg"
        ],
        "product": {
          "color": "Blue+Black"
        }
      },
      {
        "position": 3,
        "title": "Makes bathtime more productive and fun!",
        "text": "My dog is on a medicated shampoo to help cut down on itching. While it works very well in that aspect, it never really foams up the way a regular dog shampoo would. I'd have to use several handfuls of shampoo before I felt my dog was fully covered, and then it has to sit for 10 minutes, so it's always hard to tell how effective my shampooing has been. Also, my hands become covered in dog fur and shampoo suds and while that's part of the job, it's always been a little off-putting.After seeing this bath brush on Amazon, I decided to give it a try. It did an amazing job! The shampoo got extremely foamy, more sudsy than I expected, and I was able to use a lot less shampoo in our next bath. While I still got hair and shampoo on my hands, there wasn't as much. We'll definitely use this next bath! I have a corgi, so this was not too harsh on his undercoat, but also able to get through his fur. A longer-haired dog might need a little more effort in getting down to the skin.",
        "rating": 5,
        "date": "September 21, 2025",
        "author": "ShortCorgiGuy",
        "author_link": "https://www.amazon.com/gp/profile/amzn1.account.AFFHTN6MEB5CKUPEJ4UUY4J4ZR2Q?ref=cm_cr_dp_d_bdcrb_top",
        "author_image": "https://m.media-amazon.com/images/S/amazon-avatars-global/default._SX48_.png",
        "product": {
          "color": "Black"
        }
      },
      {
        "position": 4,
        "title": "Not ideal for thick coats and challenging to hold when wet",
        "text": "I really like the two styles of bristles - one to me is more of a fast scrub lather while the other is more of an exfoliant. The quality of the plastic was more sturdy than I was anticipating which is nice if your dog has thicker fur (like our border collie). With that said, the bristles aren’t long enough in my opinion for dogs with super thick fur like a German Shepard. I am also reducing a star because it’s somewhat challenging to grip and remain gripping it when it’s wet and you’re trying to go in circles or use around the sides or under your dog. Would be nice if it had some sort of handle to go over the back or side of your hand (but I imagine it wouldn’t be able to be 2 sided in that case). Also the more exfoliant side bristles are shorter than the other side as you can see from my pics.",
        "rating": 3,
        "date": "October 13, 2025",
        "author": "Schellay",
        "author_link": "https://www.amazon.com/gp/profile/amzn1.account.AHS4S7CBX3SBN2NH5YABUHONLGVQ?ref=cm_cr_dp_d_bdcrb_top",
        "author_image": "https://m.media-amazon.com/images/S/amazon-avatars-global/default._SX48_.png",
